+# APEX Sales Campaigns + Telnyx Missions
+
+Implemented from the Telnyx documentation reviewed on 2026-09-15.
+
+## What changed
+
+- Added a dedicated **Business → Sales Campaigns** dashboard section.
+- Kept **Lead Campaigns** separate from sales outreach.
+- Added `/api/sales-campaigns` for a combined email + voice control-plane view.
+- Email campaigns now expose operator pause/resume/cancel controls from the dashboard.
+- Added a provider-boundary Telnyx Missions client in `packages/core/src/telnyx-missions.ts`.
+- Added live Telnyx mission/run monitoring and pause/resume/cancel controls.
+- Added an authenticated API endpoint to create a managed Telnyx Mission and start its first run.
+- Added Telnyx to the Settings integration catalog.
+- Reused the existing `TELNYX_API_KEY`; no secret is committed.
+
+## Architecture
+
+APEX remains the control plane. Resend remains the email delivery provider. Telnyx is treated as a voice execution provider.
+
+The dashboard reads:
+- APEX `email_campaigns` + `email_sends` for email.
+- Telnyx AI Missions + recent Mission runs for voice.
+
+Telnyx mission IDs and run IDs are provider identifiers, not replacements for APEX campaign identity.
+
+## Endpoints
+
+- `GET /api/sales-campaigns`
+- `POST /api/sales-campaigns/email/:id/pause`
+- `POST /api/sales-campaigns/email/:id/resume`
+- `POST /api/sales-campaigns/email/:id/cancel`
+- `POST /api/sales-campaigns/voice`
+- `POST /api/sales-campaigns/voice/:missionId/:runId/pause`
+- `POST /api/sales-campaigns/voice/:missionId/:runId/resume`
+- `POST /api/sales-campaigns/voice/:missionId/:runId/cancel`
+
+## Verification performed here
+
+All modified TypeScript/TSX files were parsed/transpiled with the installed TypeScript compiler and produced no syntax diagnostics.
+
+A full workspace typecheck could not be run in this isolated runtime because this copy of the repository does not include workspace `node_modules`, and Corepack could not download pnpm because external package-registry DNS access is unavailable. Run the repository's normal `pnpm run typecheck:production` after installing dependencies.
+
+## Production activation
+
+1. Set `TELNYX_API_KEY` through APEX Settings or the production secret/environment system.
+2. Deploy through the repository's documented Cloud Run release path.
+3. Open **Business → Sales Campaigns**.
+4. Confirm existing Resend email campaigns appear.
+5. Confirm Telnyx connectivity shows configured.
+6. Start with a 2–3-call Telnyx Mission and verify pause/resume/cancel and result visibility before increasing volume.
